+# Shipped surface notes
+
+Task 001 capture of the shipped surfaces that the DS previews must mirror.
+
+## Sources inspected
+
+- `web/lib/memba_web/router.ex`
+- `web/lib/memba_web/live/member_invitation_live/new.ex`
+- `web/lib/memba_web/live/admin/club_member_invitations_live/new.ex`
+- `web/lib/memba_web/controllers/club_member_invitation_controller.ex`
+- `web/lib/memba_web/controllers/club_member_invitation_html/profile.html.heex`
+- `web/lib/memba_web/live/auth_live/sign_in.ex`
+- `web/lib/memba/accounts/auth_email_request.ex`
+- Focused tests for invitation, profile completion, and auth-email progress.
+
+## Invite a member — member-admin variant
+
+- Route: `/members/invitations/new`, scoped by the club host/live session.
+- Page wrapper: club-site member shell.
+- Main IDs/attributes:
+  - `#member-club-invitation-new`
+  - `data-live-view="member-club-invitation-new"`
+  - `data-club-id`
+  - `data-current-member-id`
+  - `data-active-member-count`
+- Header card copy:
+  - Back link: `Club home`
+  - Eyebrow: `Member invitations`
+  - H1: `Invite a member`
+  - Club label: selected club name in uppercase primary text.
+  - Body: `Send a one-use invitation link for {club}. The invitation stays scoped to this club, and invited people will become ordinary members after they accept.`
+- Current-member context chip/card:
+  - Avatar initials from the current member name, fallback `ME`.
+  - Name fallback: `Current member`.
+  - Subcopy: `Inviting from this club membership`.
+- Form card copy:
+  - Eyebrow: `Invitation details`
+  - H2: `Email-only member invitation`
+  - Body: `Enter the invitee's email address. Memba sends a one-use link so the invited person controls that email before membership starts.`
+- Form:
+  - Form ID: `#member-club-invitation-form`
+  - `aria-label="Invite member"`
+  - One field only: required email input.
+  - Input ID: `#member-club-invitation-email-input`
+  - Label: `Email address`
+  - `aria-label="Invitee email address"`
+  - `autocomplete="email"`
+  - Placeholder: `dana@example.com`
+  - Buttons: primary `Send invitation`, secondary `Cancel`.
+- User-visible states/copy:
+  - Invalid email: field error `Enter a valid email address.`
+  - Successful first invite: flash `Invitation sent to {normalized_email}`.
+  - Duplicate pending invite resend: flash `Invitation resent to {normalized_email}`.
+  - Already active member: flash error `That email address is already an active member of this club.`
+  - Email configuration failure: `Invitation was created, but Memba could not send the email. Check auth email delivery configuration and try again.`
+  - Email delivery failure: `Invitation was created, but Memba could not send the email. Try again.`
+
+## Invite a member — staff/admin variant
+
+- Route: `/admin/clubs/:club_id/invitations/new`.
+- Page wrapper: admin shell with active section `:clubs`.
+- Main IDs/attributes:
+  - `#club-member-invitation-new`
+  - `data-admin-page="club-member-invitation-new"`
+  - `data-club-id`
+- Header copy:
+  - Back link: `← Club`
+  - Eyebrow: `Member invitations`
+  - H1: `Invite a member`
+  - Body: `Send a one-use invitation link for {club}. The invitee controls the email address and will enter their own profile details before membership starts.`
+- Context card:
+  - Eyebrow: `Club context`
+  - Shows club name and club ID.
+- Form card copy:
+  - Eyebrow: `Invitation details`
+  - H2: `Email-only member invitation`
+  - Body: `Staff provide only the email address. Memba will not create a person record or an active club membership until the invitee accepts and completes profile details.`
+- Form:
+  - Form ID: `#club-member-invitation-form`
+  - `aria-label="Invite member"`
+  - One field only: required email input.
+  - Input ID: `#club-member-invitation-email-input`
+  - Label: `Email address`
+  - `aria-label="Invitee email address"`
+  - `autocomplete="email"`
+  - Placeholder: `robin@example.com`
+  - Buttons/links: `Send invitation`, `Cancel`.
+- User-visible states/copy:
+  - Invalid email: field error `Enter a valid email address.`
+  - Successful first invite: flash `Invitation sent to {normalized_email}`.
+  - Duplicate pending invite resend: flash `Invitation resent to {normalized_email}`.
+  - Already active member: flash error `That email address is already an active member of this club.`
+  - Missing club state: page H1 `Club not found`, body `No projected club exists for this URL.`, back link `← Clubs`.
+  - Email configuration failure: `Invitation was created, but Memba could not send the email. Check auth email delivery configuration and try again.`
+  - Email delivery failure: `Invitation was created, but Memba could not send the email. Try again.`
+
+## Invited-member profile completion
+
+- Routes:
+  - Invitation callback: `/invitations/club-members/:token`
+  - Profile form: `GET /invitations/club-members/profile`
+  - Profile submit: `POST /invitations/club-members/profile`
+- Page wrapper: app shell.
+- Main IDs/attributes:
+  - `#club-member-profile-completion`
+  - `data-club-id`
+- Header copy:
+  - Eyebrow: `Member invitation`
+  - H1: `Tell us your name`
+  - Body: `You’re accepting an invitation to join {club}. We’ll use your name and {email} to create your member profile before your membership starts.`
+- Form:
+  - Form ID: `#club-member-profile-completion-form`
+  - `aria-label="Complete your profile"`
+  - Action: `/invitations/club-members/profile`
+  - Method: `post`
+  - One field only: required text input for name.
+  - Input ID: `#club-member-profile-name-input`
+  - Field name: `profile[name]`
+  - Label: `Your name`
+  - `autocomplete="name"`
+  - Placeholder: `Robin Example`
+  - Button: `Join {club}`
+- User-visible states/copy:
+  - Starting profile completion sets flash `Finish your profile to join {club}.` or fallback `Finish your profile to accept this invitation.`
+  - Blank/invalid name keeps the invitee on the form with status 422, flash and field error `Please tell us your name.`
+  - Accepted profile redirects to the invited club with flash `Welcome to {club}.` or fallback `Welcome to Memba.`
+  - Missing/invalid profile journey redirects to `/auth` with `Follow your invitation link before completing your profile.`
+  - Invalid invitation link redirects to `/auth` with `That invitation link is no longer valid. Please ask for a new invitation.`
+
+## Sign in / check email / auth-email progress
+
+- Routes:
+  - Sign in form: `/auth`
+  - Neutral check-email page: `/auth/check-email`
+  - Request-specific progress page: `/auth/check-email/:request_id`
+  - Magic-link callback: `/auth/sign-in/:token`
+- Sign-in form copy:
+  - Eyebrow: `Sign in`
+  - H1: `Sign in with your email.`
+  - Body: `Use the email address your club or group has for you. We’ll email you a private sign-in link.`
+  - Privacy note: `To protect member privacy, this page does not say whether that email address is on a club list.`
+- Sign-in form:
+  - Form ID: `#sign-in-link-form`
+  - One required email field.
+  - Input ID: `#auth_email_input`
+  - Label: `Email address`
+  - `autocomplete="email"`
+  - Placeholder: `you@example.com`
+  - Button: `Email me a sign-in link`
+- Check-email page copy:
+  - Section ID: `#auth-sign-in-sent`
+  - Eyebrow: `Check your email`
+  - H1: `Check your email for the sign-in link.`
+  - Initial notice: `If that email address can sign in to Memba, the sign-in email is on its way.`
+  - Body: `Open the email on this iPad and tap the sign-in button. The link works once and expires in 15 minutes. If it does not arrive, check your junk mail or ask for another link.`
+  - Secondary link: `Ask for another sign-in link`
+- Progress panel:
+  - Panel ID: `#auth-email-progress`
+  - Eyebrow: `Sign-in link progress`
+  - Message ID: `#auth-email-progress-message`
+- Persisted progress statuses:
+  - `created`
+  - `sent`
+  - `provider_accepted`
+  - `provider_delayed`
+  - `provider_failed`
+- User-visible progress message mapping:
+  - No request ID / invalid request: `If that email address can sign in to Memba, the sign-in email is on its way.`
+  - `created`: `Preparing your sign-in link…`
+  - `sent`, before the 60-second fallback threshold: `If this email can sign in, the link is on its way.`
+  - `provider_accepted`: `Your mailbox provider has accepted the email. It should appear shortly.`
+  - `provider_delayed` / `provider_failed`: no provider-specific problem is exposed; before 60 seconds the page stays neutral and after 60 seconds uses the fallback guidance.
+  - 60 seconds without provider acceptance: `If it does not arrive, check junk mail or ask for another link.`
+  - Expired user-facing progress: `This sign-in-link request has expired. Ask for another link.`
+- Privacy behaviour to preserve in previews:
+  - Known and unknown emails use the same route shape and neutral first response.
+  - Unknown emails do not receive a fake `provider_accepted` state.
+  - The UI must not claim the email is in the inbox; it says the mailbox provider accepted it.
